-- ============================================================================
-- T5 - Digital Services Act: online platform
-- Instrument : Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 (Digital Services Act)
--              http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj
-- Pinpoint   : Art 3(g)(iii), Art 3(i), Art 3(k); Recital 14
-- Version    : OJ L 277, 27.10.2022, p. 1 (original text) - NOT CHECKED. EUR-Lex was
--              blocked from the spike environment, so the text below is quoted from
--              the author's knowledge and must be verified before reliance.
-- Evaluated  : 2026-09-23
-- Operative text (UNVERIFIED):
--   Art 3(g)(iii): a 'hosting' service, consisting of the storage of information
--     provided by, and at the request of, a recipient of the service;
--   Art 3(i): 'online platform' means a hosting service that, at the request of a
--     recipient of the service, stores and disseminates information to the public,
--     unless that activity is a minor and purely ancillary feature of another
--     service or a minor functionality of the principal service and, for objective
--     and technical reasons, cannot be used without that other service, and the
--     integration of the feature or functionality into the other service is not a
--     means to circumvent the applicability of this Regulation;
--   Art 3(k): 'dissemination to the public' means making information available, at
--     the request of the recipient of the service who provided the information, to
--     a potentially unlimited number of third parties;
--   Recital 14 (extract): ... Interpersonal communication services ..., such as
--     emails or private messaging services, fall outside the scope of the
--     definition of online platforms as they are used for interpersonal
--     communication between a finite number of persons determined by the sender
--     of the communication. However, the obligations ... can apply to services
--     that allow the making available of information to a potentially unlimited
--     number of recipients, not determined by the sender of the communication,
--     such as through public groups or open channels.
-- Modelling:
--   * "is a hosting service": a recorded judgement wins; otherwise derived from the
--     fact "stores user content at the recipient's request".
--   * "disseminates to the public": a recorded judgement wins; otherwise derived
--     ONLY in the clear case (public posting => yes). No public posting is NOT
--     treated as "no", because closed groups with automatic admission can still be
--     dissemination to the public (Recital 14).
--   * The ancillary exception is always a judgement input.
-- ============================================================================

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT kleene

§ `DSA Art 3(i) and 3(k) - online platform`
@ref-map dsa-art3 https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj#art_3

@ref dsa-art3 Art 3(g)(iii)
GIVEN `hosting service judgement`         IS A Judgement
      `stores user content at request`    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a hosting service` MEANS
    `first known of` (`the answer to` `hosting service judgement`)
                     `stores user content at request`

@ref dsa-art3 Art 3(k) and Recital 14
GIVEN `dissemination judgement` IS A Judgement
      `public posting`          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`disseminates to the public` MEANS
    `first known of` (`the answer to` `dissemination judgement`)
                     (`yes if` `public posting`)

@export The service is an online platform under DSA Art 3(i). Returns yes, no or undetermined (null).
@ref dsa-art3 Art 3(i)
GIVEN `hosting service judgement`         IS A Judgement      @desc Art 3(g)(iii) judgement, if one was made
      `stores user content at request`    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc fact: stores information provided by and at the request of users
      `dissemination judgement`           IS A Judgement      @desc Art 3(k) judgement, if one was made
      `public posting`                    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc fact: users can post publicly
      `minor ancillary exception`         IS A Judgement      @desc Art 3(i) exception judgement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an online platform` MEANS
    `all of` (LIST (`is a hosting service` `hosting service judgement` `stores user content at request`)
                   (`disseminates to the public` `dissemination judgement` `public posting`)
                   (`not` (`the answer to` `minor ancillary exception`)))
